## Prove you broke nothing — before and after

<The thing at risk> is the thing at risk, so measure it, don't hope.

**Before you change anything**, record:

```bash
<the exact command, loop or one-liner — the SAME text that appears below>
```

**After <the change / the reload>**, run the **identical** command and compare. If <any value>
changed, you broke something — <the revert step>, and report. **Put both readings in your report
verbatim**, not a summary of them.

Then prove your own work. Run this **before** you start and confirm it fails:

```bash
<command that establishes your change is live, with an expected value>
```

