## Appendix — for a diagnostic brief

### How it is wired

<The map. Component → file → element → handler. No instructions in this block; it is reference,
and mixing it with the procedure is what makes bug reports unusable.>

### Diagnostic procedure — in this order, changing nothing

1. `<command or console expression>` → record the raw value.
2. `<command>` → record the raw value.

### What each reading means

| Reading | Meaning |
|---|---|
| <`d` is empty> | <calc() never completes> |
| <`d` has a value but never changes> | <the handlers are not firing> |
| <`__probe` is undefined after the switch> | <the node was REPLACED — stale refs, not handlers> |

**Report the raw values, not your interpretation of them.** <If the test is inconclusive, say so
— "I could not separate the two causes" is a useful result and a guess is not.>

**The decision point on a diagnostic brief is the stop-gate itself:** report before changing
anything.

